                <pb facs="0216" n="114" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg114"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">803.01 Manchuria/781: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-01-19T12:00:00+08:00">January 19,
                        1933—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 19—1:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>62. Following from American Consul General at Harbin: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 18, 1 p.m. Returned this morning Harbin from Barga which is
                            quiet and dominated by Japanese military and civil officials. Chinese
                            influence appears entirely eliminated. Older Mongol princes seemed
                            pleased. They and Japanese officials treated me most hospitably”.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
